{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3151","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-sam-task-file-language.md@sha256:c0eec33226bd3b25bb5891e5d6397bd86cae621cd5b8df2bc5eed1dab9d5310b"},"owner_reference":"3151","content":"# Architecture Spec: Remove file-based SAM-task language (#3151)\n\n## Scope recap\n\nA SAM task is identified by address (`P{id}/T{id}`), never a file, except inside the\nlocal-YAML `ContextBackend`/`TaskBackend`, where file storage is genuinely correct. This spec\ndesigns the structural fix (model, backends, hook consumer, tests, required-reading) that must\nland and pass CI before the ~43-file prose sweep starts. No implementation is included below \u2014\nthis is WHAT to build, for Phase 4 task decomposition to turn into SAM tasks.\n\nGrounding: all code claims below were verified directly against\n`plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py`,\n`sam_schema/core/backends/{local_context_backend,memory_context_backend,github_context_backend,beads}.py`,\n`sam_schema/core/context_backend.py`, `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/{task_status_hook,implementation_manager}.py`,\n`tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py`, and `AGENTS.md` in this session (not\ncarried over from the Impact Radius summary alone).\n\n---\n\n## 1. `ActiveTaskContext` model (`sam_schema/core/models.py:737-771`)\n\n### Decision: make `task_file_path` optional, not a subtype split\n\n```python\ntask_file_path: str | None = Field(\n    default=None,\n    description=(\n        \"Absolute path to the plan YAML file containing this task. \"\n        \"Populated only by the local-YAML ContextBackend; None for memory, GitHub, and beads.\"\n    ),\n)\n```\n\n### Why optional, not a `LocalActiveTaskContext` subtype\n\nThe `ContextBackend` Protocol (`sam_schema/core/context_backend.py:52-67`) declares one\nsignature for all four backends:\n\n```python\ndef set_active_task(\n    self, session_id: str, plan: str, task: str, plan_dir: str,\n    parent_issue_number: str | int | None = None,\n) -> ActiveTaskContext: ...\n```\n\nEvery implementation returns a bare `ActiveTaskContext`, and every consumer (`task_status_hook.py`,\nthe MCP `sam_active_task` surface, `get_active_task`/`list_active_tasks`) is typed against that\none return type. A subtype (`LocalActiveTaskContext(ActiveTaskContext)` with `task_file_path: str`\nrequired) would force every one of those call sites into a `ActiveTaskContext | LocalActiveTaskContext`\nunion or an `isinstance` narrowing step, for a field that already defaults cleanly to `None` with\nno cross-field invariant to protect (nothing computed from `task_file_path` elsewhere in the\nmodel). Ladder verdict: `str | None = None` is the one-line fix; a Protocol/subtype split is\nunrequested structure for a field three of four backends never had a use for.\n\n`plan: str | None` and `task: str | None` (already additive fields, `models.py:751-757`) become\nthe canonical address. Do **not** tighten these to required in this pass \u2014 every backend already\nsets both unconditionally in `set_active_task`, but old on-disk `active-task-{session_id}.json`\nfiles written before these fields existed (crashed sessions, stale files) would fail\n`model_validate` if they became required. That tightening is a separate, independently-decidable\nchange; out of scope here (no consumer needs it to be required to fix this issue).\n\n### Docstring correction (contract-adjacent, not cosmetic)\n\nCurrent class docstring: *\"Session-to-task binding stored in context_dir() as\nactive-task-{session_id}.json. The SubagentStop hook reads this file directly from the\nfilesystem.\"* This is only true for the local backend \u2014 the file at `context_dir()/...` is\nwritten exclusively by `LocalContextBackend.set_active_task`; memory/GitHub/beads never write it,\nand the hook's primary retrieval path is the `sam_active_task(action=\"get\")` fastmcp call (see\n\u00a73), with the file read as a fallback that is only ever populated for the local backend. Task:\ncorrect the docstring to state the binding is identified by `(plan, task)` address across all\nbackends, and that `context_dir()` file persistence is a local-backend-specific storage detail,\nnot a universal contract.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The three fabricating backends\n\nAll three currently build `ActiveTaskContext(task_file_path=<fabricated>, task_id=task, plan=plan,\ntask=task, plan_dir=plan_dir, parent_issue_number=..., session_id=..., started_at=...)`. Fix per\nfile:\n\n| File | Current | Change |\n|---|---|---|\n| `memory_context_backend.py:59` | `task_file_path=f\"{plan_dir}/{plan}.yaml\"` | Delete the kwarg. Constructor relies on the new `None` default. |\n| `github_context_backend.py:181` (uses `_resolve_task_file_path` defined at ~`:350`) | `task_file_path=_resolve_task_file_path(plan, plan_dir)` | Delete the kwarg. Delete the now-unused module-level `_resolve_task_file_path` helper (confirmed single call site). |\n| `beads.py:1306` (uses `_resolve_task_file_path` defined at ~`:1388`) | `task_file_path=task_file_path` (locally computed via the module-level helper) | Delete the kwarg and the local `task_file_path = _resolve_task_file_path(...)` line. Delete the now-unused module-level `_resolve_task_file_path` helper (confirmed single call site). |\n\n`local_context_backend.py:72,128` is unchanged \u2014 it has its own `_resolve_task_file_path`\n*static method* (distinct symbol, no naming collision with the module-level helpers being\ndeleted elsewhere) and continues to populate a genuine path. This is the Anti-Goal-1 boundary:\nverified correct, not touched.\n\nDownstream effect verified safe: `github_context_backend.py` and `beads.py` both serialize the\ncontext via `context.model_dump(exclude_none=False)` (comment body / `bd remember` payload) and\ndeserialize via `ActiveTaskContext.model_validate(data)`. With `task_file_path` optional, the\ndump includes `\"task_file_path\": null` and validation round-trips cleanly \u2014 no serialization\ncontract to renegotiate.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Consumers\n\n### `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`\n\nTwo independent retrieval paths currently derive a *plan address* from a *path string* via\n`_extract_plan_addr_from_path()` (regex `(P[0-9a-f]+)` against the filename) \u2014 this only ever\nworked because the fabricated paths in memory/github/beads happened to embed the address in the\nfilename. Once `task_file_path` is `None` for those three backends, this regex silently returns\n`None` for every non-local session \u2014 this is the concrete break that makes the ordering\nconstraint (\u00a77) non-optional, not just tidy sequencing.\n\nFix: read the `plan`/`task` fields directly; delete the path-parsing indirection entirely.\n\n- `read_task_context()` (`:304-329`) \u2014 currently: `context_data.get(\"task_file_path\")` +\n  `context_data.get(\"task_id\")`, returns `(task_file, task_id)` where callers later resolve the\n  address out of `task_file`. Change: read `context_data.get(\"plan\")` and\n  `context_data.get(\"task_id\")` directly; return `(plan_addr, task_id)`. Update the docstring's\n  return-tuple description from *\"(plan_id_or_path, task_id) ... raw string value ... plan\n  address or filesystem path\"* to *\"(plan_address, task_id)\"* \u2014 the ambiguity this docstring is\n  hedging against no longer exists once the field itself is unambiguous.\n- `_call_sam_active_task_get()` (`:331-370`) \u2014 currently: `active.get(\"task_file_path\")`. Change:\n  `active.get(\"plan\")`. Same docstring correction (drop \"raw string value... path or address\").\n- `_read_context_file()` (`:712-731`) \u2014 currently: `data.get(\"task_file_path\")`. Change:\n  `data.get(\"plan\")`.\n- `_extract_plan_addr_from_path()` (`:457-469`) and its three call sites (`:835, :911, :968`) \u2014\n  delete the function entirely once all three callers are updated to consume the address value\n  directly instead of parsing it out of a path. A regex-based address extractor with zero\n  remaining callers is dead code, not a fallback worth keeping.\n\nNet effect: the hook stops caring whether a path was ever involved; it reads an address field\nthat every backend (including local) already populates via `plan`/`task`.\n\n### `implementation_manager.py:1354-1371` (`claim_task` Typer command) \u2014 different concern, no change\n\nVerified via repo-wide grep (`grep -rn \"task_file_path\"`, restricted to non-test files): this\ncommand's `task_file_path` is its **own CLI positional argument** (`exists=True, resolve_path=True`),\nused to instantiate `LocalYamlTaskProvider(task_file_path.parent)` directly. It never reads\n`ActiveTaskContext` \u2014 no `.get(\"task_file_path\")`, no JSON payload involved. This is a\nlocal-YAML-only entry point and is correctly excluded from this refactor under Anti-Goal 1.\n\nVerified separately: no skill or agent file in `plugins/development-harness` currently invokes\n`implementation-manager.py claim-task` (grep across `skills/`, `agents/`, `docs/` found only\ngenerated-artifact JSON, not a live call site). Task requirement, not a code change: add a\nverification step confirming no dispatch path feeds this argument a value sourced from\n`ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path` (which would silently receive `None` for non-local backends\npost-fix). If such a caller is found, it must resolve the local plan file path independently\n(mirroring `LocalContextBackend._resolve_task_file_path`), not trust a context field that no\nlonger carries it for three of four backends.\n\n### `hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 confirmed unaffected\n\nDispatches on hook event name and matcher (`PostToolUse` \u2192 `Write|Edit|Bash`; `SubagentStop` \u2192\n`^task-worker$`), never on a payload field name. No change. Add a manual smoke-test step\n(dispatch one task through `PostToolUse` and one `SubagentStop` after the field rename lands) as\na task acceptance check, not a code edit.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` retirement and `AGENTS.md` required reading\n\n### `AGENTS.md` edits (verified exact locations this session)\n\n- **Required Reading section** (`AGENTS.md` \"Modifying data structures, domain models, or\n  task/plan schemas\"): delete the bullet `Load [Task File Format](./docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md) \u2014\n  field reference, authorized writers, sam CLI usage. **Drift warning**...`. Keep the\n  `[Domain model source](./sam_schema/core/models.py)` bullet (already the stated source of\n  truth) and the `[Workflow Architecture Diagram]` bullet \u2014 between the two, no replacement\n  reading is needed; nothing in `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` is authoritative that isn't already covered\n  by `models.py` (fields) and the workflow diagram (data flow/state machine).\n- **Inline cross-reference in the SAM Plan section** (~line 114): *\"See\n  [docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md](./docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md) 'DH CLI Usage Guide' for the full\n  grouped-command reference.\"* \u2014 delete this sentence. The three sentences immediately above it\n  already give the full CLI-equivalent sequence (`plan create` \u2192 `plan append-task` \u2192 `plan\n  finalize`); nothing is lost by dropping the cross-reference.\n- **Documentation Update Triggers table** row *\"Data structure change... | Yes \u2014 update\n  `models.py` first, then Task File Format\"* \u2192 *\"Yes \u2014 update `models.py` first\"*.\n\n### File retirement\n\n- `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` (577 lines): before deleting, extract anything not already\n  duplicated elsewhere. Verified this session: its \"DH CLI Usage Guide\" content\n  (`sam_plan`/`sam_task` grouped-command sequences) is already substantially present in\n  `AGENTS.md`'s own SAM Plan section. Task requirement: diff the two, fold any CLI-usage-guide\n  content that is *not* already in `AGENTS.md` or the `dh:dh-meta-docs` skill references into\n  `skills/dh-meta-docs/references/` (the existing canonical home for pipeline/operations\n  reference material \u2014 reuse it, don't create a new doc), then delete\n  `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`.\n- `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md`: verified directly this session \u2014 this is a\n  7-line redirect stub pointing at `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`, not an active duplicate (the\n  Impact Radius's REFUTE of \"delete the layer-0 duplicate\" is correct as far as it goes: there is\n  no *duplicate content* to reconcile). But once the canonical file it redirects to is deleted,\n  the stub becomes a dangling link \u2014 delete it in the same task as the canonical file, as a\n  trivial follow-on. (Flagged in Concerns: the Impact Radius phrasing \"nothing to delete\" is\n  correct only pre-retirement and should not be read as \"leave the stub in place forever.\")\n\n### The 10 (11, including the layer-0 stub) documents linking to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`\n\n`docs/backend-providers.md`, `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`,\n`docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md`, `docs/beads-and-workflow-usage.md`,\n`docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`, `docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md`,\n`docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/README.md`, `skills/evaluate-sdlc-layers/SKILL.md`,\n`skills/dh-meta-docs/references/artifact-conventions.md`,\n`skills/dh-meta-docs/references/default-development-flow.md`. Each link goes dead once the file\nis deleted. These are folded into prose-sweep Group D (\u00a76) \u2014 but that group **must** run after\nthis section's deletion task completes, not before, or the link-repair edits would target a file\nstill scheduled for deletion and need re-touching.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Generalizing `tests_backlog/test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py`\n\nCurrent precedent (`:75-79`):\n\n```python\ndef test_sam_server_has_no_task_backend_routing() -> None:\n    assert \"sam_schema.core.task_config\" not in _imports(sam_server)\n    source = _source(sam_server)\n    assert \"create_task_backend\" not in source\n    assert \"task_file_path\" not in source\n```\n\nThe file's existing `_source(module)` helper (`:12-15`, reads a module's file via `Path.read_text`)\nis reused as-is \u2014 no new helper needed. Add one parametrized test covering the three fabricating\nbackend modules, matching pytest idiom even though this file doesn't currently use\n`pytest.mark.parametrize` elsewhere (three near-duplicate flat `test_*` functions would be more\nrepetitive than one parametrized test; parametrize is standard pytest, not novel structure):\n\n```python\nimport sam_schema.core.backends.beads as beads_backend\nimport sam_schema.core.backends.github_context_backend as github_context_backend\nimport sam_schema.core.backends.memory_context_backend as memory_context_backend\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"module\", [memory_context_backend, github_context_backend, beads_backend]\n)\ndef test_non_local_context_backend_has_no_task_file_path(module: ModuleType) -> None:\n    assert \"task_file_path\" not in _source(module)\n```\n\nExplicitly **excluded** from this assertion (must keep the string, don't regress-test them):\n`local_context_backend.py` (genuine file path, must keep `_resolve_task_file_path` and the\n`task_file_path=` kwarg) and `sam_schema/core/models.py` (the field's declaration site). This\nscoping should be a one-line comment at the test, not a separate doc.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Prose sweep decomposition (Phase 4 input \u2014 do not write the prose here)\n\n~43 in-scope files (57 total \"task file\" hits minus ~14 legitimate local-YAML/legacy-migration\nfiles, per the Impact Radius's own count) group into 4 task-decomposition units by\ndirectory/pattern homogeneity, not 43 individual tasks:\n\n**Group B \u2014 `agents/*.md` (5 files):** `code-reviewer.md`, `dh-context-gathering.md`,\n`feature-verifier.md`, `integration-checker.md`, `plan-validator.md`. Pattern: \"SAM task file\" /\n\"the task file\" \u2192 \"SAM task\" / \"the task\"; where an operation is named correctly but the noun is\nwrong, fix only the noun.\nExample: `agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 before: *\"Read the SAM task file using\n`mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\"* \u2192 after: *\"Read the SAM task using `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_task`\"*\n(the operation name was already correct; only \"file\" is wrong).\n\n**Group C \u2014 `skills/*/SKILL.md` (10 files):** `clear-cove-task-design`, `dh-meta-docs`,\n`dispatch`, `execution`, `final-verification`, `forensic-review`, `generate-task`,\n`implementation-manager`, `interop`, `start-task`. Pattern: workflow steps titled \"Read Task\nFile\" \u2192 \"Read Task\"; documented parameters named `task_file_path` \u2192 the address pair\n(`plan`, `task`).\nExample: `skills/execution/SKILL.md` \u2014 before: workflow step *\"Read Task File\"* \u2192 after: *\"Read\nTask (`sam_task` action=read)\"*.\nExample: `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` \u2014 before: documented parameter `task_file_path` \u2192\nafter: documented parameters `plan`, `task` (address pair, matching the corrected hook payload\nfrom \u00a73).\n\n**Group D \u2014 general docs + dead-link repair (~20 files), gated on \u00a74's deletion task:**\n`CONTEXT.md`, `README.md`, `docs/backlog-lifecycle.draft.md`,\n`docs/complexity-fit-and-economics-of-agents.md`, `docs/sdlc-layers/layer-1/layer-1-overview.md`,\n`docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md`,\n`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/interactive-browser.md`, plus the 11\ndead-link documents from \u00a74. Pattern: \"task file\" \u2192 \"task\" or \"SAM task\" per grammatical context;\nany link to `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` is removed or repointed to `sam_schema/core/models.py`.\nExample: `docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 before: *\"see Task File Format for field reference\"* \u2192\nafter: *\"see `sam_schema/core/models.py` for field reference\"*.\n\n**Group E \u2014 schema-defining reference docs (2 files), precise correction not mechanical\nfind-replace:** `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` and\n`skills/dh-meta-docs/references/language-manifest-schema.md`. These define a field's *meaning*,\nnot incidental prose, so each needs a specific rewrite rather than a pattern substitution.\nExample: `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` \u2014 before: *\"`plan`: relative path to SAM\ntask file\"* \u2192 after: *\"`plan`: SAM plan address (e.g. `P1601`)\"*.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Task ordering / dependency structure\n\nOne plan, internal task dependencies \u2014 not split plans, per this session's instruction.\n\n```\nStructural tier (must ALL complete + pass CI before Prose tier starts):\n  T1  models.py \u2014 task_file_path optional, docstring correction           [no deps]\n  T2  3 fabricating backends (memory, github, beads) cleanup              [depends: T1]\n  T3  task_status_hook.py consumer fix + dead-code removal                [depends: T1, T2]\n  T4  AGENTS.md required-reading edit + TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md/layer-0 stub  [depends: T1]\n      retirement (content-diff-and-fold into dh-meta-docs first)\n  T5  Generalize test_high_level_storage_boundaries.py                    [depends: T2]\n  T6  Verification: claim_task CLI argument not fed from                 [depends: T1, T3]\n      ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path anywhere in the dispatch path;\n      hooks.json PostToolUse/SubagentStop smoke test\n\nProse tier (each group depends on the full structural tier, i.e. T1-T6):\n  T7  Group B \u2014 agents/*.md (5 files)                                    [depends: T1-T6]\n  T8  Group C \u2014 skills/*/SKILL.md (10 files)                             [depends: T1-T6]\n  T9  Group D \u2014 general docs + dead-link repair (~20 files)              [depends: T1-T6, T4]\n  T10 Group E \u2014 schema-defining reference docs (2 files)                 [depends: T1-T6]\n```\n\nT9 additionally depends on T4 specifically (not just the tier boundary) because it repairs links\nto a file T4 deletes \u2014 sequencing this within the same tier gate is necessary but not sufficient;\nT9 must not start until T4's deletion (not just T4's AGENTS.md edit) has landed, since a partial\nT4 completion (edit without deletion) would leave T9 fixing links to a file that still exists,\nsilently under-scoping the edit.\n\n---\n\n<concerns>\n1. **Model docstring is actively wrong, not just imprecise** (`models.py:737-745`): \"The\n   SubagentStop hook reads this file directly from the filesystem\" describes only the local\n   backend's fallback path; the hook's primary retrieval is the `sam_active_task` fastmcp call\n   (`task_status_hook.py:331-370`), and for memory/GitHub/beads no such file is ever written. This\n   is a structural-doc contradiction of the same species the issue is about (a docstring on the\n   fabricating field's own home model teaching the file model) \u2014 included as a required edit in\n   \u00a71, not optional polish.\n2. **Impact Radius's \"nothing to delete\" framing for the layer-0 stub is time-scoped and could\n   mislead task decomposition** if quoted verbatim: it's correct pre-retirement (no *duplicate\n   content* exists to reconcile) but becomes false once `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` is deleted (the\n   stub's redirect target vanishes, leaving a dangling link). \u00a74 makes the stub's deletion an\n   explicit part of the same task as the canonical file's deletion; a task-decomposition pass\n   reading only the Impact Radius bullet in isolation could skip it.\n3. **`implementation_manager.py:1354-1371`'s `task_file_path` is a different field than the one\n   this issue is about**, and grouping it under \"Code Producers\" in the Impact Radius (alongside\n   `models.py`, the three backends) risks a task-decomposition agent treating it as another\n   fabrication site to fix the same way. Verified this session: it's a CLI positional argument for\n   the local-YAML-only `claim_task` command, never reads `ActiveTaskContext`. \u00a73 designs it as a\n   verification-only task (confirm no caller bridges the two), not a rename.\n4. **RT-ICA condition \"no external consumer\" (repo-wide outside `plugins/development-harness`)**\n   was checked by the grooming swarm via grep, not by tracing actual call graphs into any sibling\n   plugin that might invoke `implementation-manager.py claim-task` as a subprocess from outside\n   this plugin's own tree (e.g., a CI script or another plugin's hook). Low risk given the grep\n   found zero local callers either, but worth one more repo-root-level grep (not just\n   `plugins/development-harness`) before T6 is marked done, since \"no skill calls it\" is a\n   narrower claim than \"no external caller invokes it.\"\n</concerns>\n"}